IP_NAME	Test_Case_Name	Test_Description	Test_Procedure	Register_Block	Register_Name	Register_Offset	Register_Access	Field_Name	Field_Bits	Field_Description	Write_Value	Expected_Read_Value	Validation_Criteria	Pass_Condition	Fail_Condition
LPDDR4	lpddr4_inline_ecc_1bit_data_modify_test	Verify inline ECC 1-bit correctable error detection and interrupt generation. The test configures ECC in inline mode with selective region protection (ecc_region_map=0x55), initializes memory via scrubber, writes random data through port1, reads back data and verifies that 1-bit ECC correctable errors are detected, corrected, and the corresponding interrupt is asserted for protected regions. The correctable error count is verified to be 5.	"1. Enable GIC interrupt for DDR controller (CTL_INT_NO).
2. Write SYSREG_INTR_EN_ADDR to enable controller interrupt at system level.
3. Call gpv_programming() for bus configuration.
4. Set ctl_base and phy_base addresses.
5. Configure bus_width=0 (Full Bus), DBI_EN=0, DM_EN=1, ECC_EN=1.
6. Execute lpddr4_training().
7. Enable SBR done interrupt via SII register (ctl_base+0x819C).
8. Disable SWCTL (ctl_base+0x320=0x0) for quasi-dynamic programming.
9. Write ECCCFG0 (ctl_base+0x70) with ecc_region_map=0x55 and ecc_mode=0x4 (inline ECC).
10. Write ECCCFG1 (ctl_base+0x74) with data_poison_en=1, data_poison_bit=1 (1-bit poison), ecc_region_parity_lock=1.
11. Re-enable SWCTL (ctl_base+0x320=0x1).
12. Initialize ECC-protected memory regions via scrubber (memory_init_scrb) for regions where ecc_region_map bit is set.
13. Write random 64-bit data to port1 addresses for all 7 regions.
14. Call training_done().
15. Clear ECCCTL (ctl_base+0x7C=0x0).
16. Read data from port1 base address.
17. Poll ECCSTAT (ctl_base+0x78) for ecc_corrected_err (bit[8]=1).
18. Clear corrected error via ECCCTL (ctl_base+0x7C, bit[0]=1).
19. Write SII interrupt status register (ctl_base+0x8194) to clear corrected error interrupt.
20. Enable ECC corrected error interrupt via SII (ctl_base+0x819C) and ECCCTL (ctl_base+0x7C, bit[8]=1).
21. Read data from each region via port1 and verify data matches for protected regions.
22. Wait for interrupt on protected regions; verify no interrupt on non-protected regions.
23. Read ECCERRCNT (ctl_base+0x80) and verify correctable error count equals 5.
24. Call finish(err0)."	UMCTL2_REGS	SWCTL	0x320	read-write	sw_done	[0]	Enables quasi-dynamic register programming outside reset	0x00000000 / 0x00000001	NA	Write 0 to enable quasi-dynamic programming, write 1 when done	Register accepts write without error	Write fails or value not reflected
