LPDDR4	lpddr4_inline_ecc_2bit_data_modify_test	Verify inline ECC 2-bit uncorrectable error detection and interrupt generation. The test configures ECC in inline mode with selective region protection (ecc_region_map=0x55), initializes memory via scrubber, writes random data through port1, reads back data and verifies that 2-bit ECC uncorrectable errors are detected, the corresponding interrupt is asserted for protected regions, and slave error (SLVERR) is taken. The uncorrectable error count is verified to be 5.	"1. Enable GIC interrupt for DDR controller (CTL_INT_NO).
2. Write SYSREG_INTR_EN_ADDR to enable controller interrupt at system level.
3. Call gpv_programming() for bus configuration.
4. Set ctl_base and phy_base addresses.
5. Configure bus_width=0 (Full Bus), DBI_EN=0, DM_EN=1, ECC_EN=1.
6. Execute lpddr4_training().
7. Enable SBR done interrupt via SII register (ctl_base+0x819C).
8. Disable SWCTL (ctl_base+0x320=0x0) for quasi-dynamic programming.
9. Write ECCCFG0 (ctl_base+0x70) with ecc_region_map=0x55 and ecc_mode=0x4 (inline ECC).
10. Write ECCCFG1 (ctl_base+0x74) with data_poison_en=1, data_poison_bit=0 (2-bit poison), ecc_region_parity_lock=1.
11. Re-enable SWCTL (ctl_base+0x320=0x1).
12. Initialize ECC-protected memory regions via scrubber (memory_init_scrb) for regions where ecc_region_map bit is set.
13. Write random 64-bit data to port1 addresses for all 7 regions.
14. Call training_done().
15. Clear ECCCTL (ctl_base+0x7C=0x0).
16. Read data from port1 base address.
17. Poll ECCSTAT (ctl_base+0x78) for ecc_uncorrected_err (bit[16]=1).
18. Clear uncorrected error via ECCCTL (ctl_base+0x7C, bit[1]=1).
19. Write SII interrupt status register (ctl_base+0x8194) to clear uncorrected error interrupt.
20. Enable ECC uncorrected error interrupt via SII (ctl_base+0x819C) and ECCCTL (ctl_base+0x7C, bit[9]=1).
21. Read data from each region via port1 - expect SLVERR on protected regions.
22. Wait for interrupt on protected regions; verify no interrupt on non-protected regions.
23. Read ECCERRCNT (ctl_base+0x80) and verify uncorrectable error count (bits[31:16]) equals 5.
24. Verify num_slverr_taken equals 5.
25. Call finish(err0)."	UMCTL2_REGS	SWCTL	0x320	read-write	sw_done	[0]	Enables quasi-dynamic register programming outside reset	0x00000000 / 0x00000001	NA	Write 0 to enable quasi-dynamic programming, write 1 when done	Register accepts write without error	Write fails or value not reflected
