LPDDR4	lpddr4_mem_dm_test	Verify LPDDR4 memory data masking (DM) functionality. The test configures the DDR controller with DM enabled (DM_EN=1), performs write and read operations through both port0 and port1 with random 64-bit data patterns across multiple address offsets, and verifies data integrity by comparing read-back data against expected values. Tests both fine-grained (0x1000 offset) and coarse-grained (0x20000000 offset) address patterns.	"1. Call gpv_programming() for bus configuration.
2. Set ctl_base and phy_base addresses.
3. Configure bus_width=0 (Full Bus), DBI_EN=0, DM_EN=1.
4. Execute lpddr4_training().
5. Write 10 random 64-bit values to port0 at offsets 0x0, 0x1000, 0x2000, ..., 0x9000.
6. Read back 10 values from port0 and compare against expected data.
7. Read back 10 values from port1 (same physical memory) and compare against expected data.
8. Write 32 random 64-bit values to port1 at offsets 0x0, 0x20000000, 0x40000000, ..., 0x3E0000000.
9. Read back 32 values from port1 and compare against expected data.
10. Call finish(err0)."	NA	NA	NA	NA	NA	NA	No direct UMCTL2 register accesses in this test - memory data path test only	NA	NA	All write-read data comparisons match (err0 == 0)	Any data mismatch (err0 > 0)
LPDDR4	lpddr4_mem_half_data_bus_width_test	Verify LPDDR4 memory access with half data bus width configuration. The test configures the DDR controller with bus_width=1 (Half Bus), DBI_EN=0, DM_EN=0, performs training and then reads pre-initialized memory patterns (0x3333333333333333 and 0x2222222222222222) from both port0 and port1 at offsets 0x100 and 0x108, verifying the data integrity in half bus width mode.	"1. Call gpv_programming() for bus configuration.
2. Set ctl_base and phy_base addresses.
3. Configure bus_width=1 (Half Bus), DBI_EN=0, DM_EN=0.
4. Execute lpddr4_training().
5. Call training_done().
6. Wait 1000 cycles.
7. Read 64-bit data from port0+0x100 and port0+0x108.
8. Verify port0 data: read_data0 == 0x3333333333333333 and read_data1 == 0x2222222222222222.
9. Read 64-bit data from port1+0x100 and port1+0x108.
10. Verify port1 data: read_data2 == 0x3333333333333333 and read_data3 == 0x2222222222222222.
11. Call finish(err0)."	NA	NA	NA	NA	NA	NA	No direct UMCTL2 register accesses in this test - memory data path test with half bus width	NA	NA	All read data matches expected patterns (err0 == 0): 0x3333333333333333 at offset 0x100 and 0x2222222222222222 at offset 0x108	Any data mismatch (err0 > 0)